      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 6.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, hello, doctor. I think it's my turn."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.85,
      "end_seconds": 12.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.89,
      "end_seconds": 18.94,
      "duration_seconds": 6.05,
      "text": "So, I've been getting out of puff on the stairs, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.85,
      "end_seconds": 23.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Okay, how long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.1,
      "end_seconds": 27.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Uh, I've had it since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.87,
      "end_seconds": 37.2,
      "duration_seconds": 8.33,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.28,
      "end_seconds": 42.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Mostly moderate. It's every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.95,
      "end_seconds": 46.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Do you have any medical conditions I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.14,
      "end_seconds": 50.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "No, nothing at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.34,
      "end_seconds": 55.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.24,
      "end_seconds": 63.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "Okay, so no, nothing as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.61,
      "end_seconds": 73.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.12,
      "end_seconds": 80.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.23,
      "end_seconds": 83.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.27,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.36,
      "end_seconds": 87.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.08,
      "end_seconds": 103.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Do you take any regular medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.15,
      "end_seconds": 107.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Nothing regular, uh, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.53,
      "end_seconds": 112.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Any palpitations, calf swelling or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.3,
      "end_seconds": 118.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Okay, so no, no palpitations, calf swelling or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.8,
      "end_seconds": 121.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "What about chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.03,
      "end_seconds": 124.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Definitely no chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.99,
      "end_seconds": 128.71,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.2,
      "end_seconds": 134.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "Ah, uh, no, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 135.76,
      "end_seconds": 138.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.75,
      "end_seconds": 148.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.14,
      "end_seconds": 171.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.81,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 120 over 74, temp 36.7 degrees, pulse is 82 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.11,
      "end_seconds": 176.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.18,
      "end_seconds": 178.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.65,
      "end_seconds": 198.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.93,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and the chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.41,
      "end_seconds": 207.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.05,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.07,
      "end_seconds": 218.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "You can relax now. Okay, thinking it through, this looks most like breathlessness with several possible contributors."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.74,
      "end_seconds": 225.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.03,
      "end_seconds": 236.89,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like breathlessness with several possible contributors, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.83,
      "end_seconds": 287.27,
      "duration_seconds": 31.44,
      "text": "I'll request an echocardiogram, it'll help with breathlessness. A short daily walk, building up slowly, is a sensible start. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed. If it hasn't settled in a month, we'd think about blood tests, but not now. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.19,
      "end_seconds": 293.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Alright, I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.1,
      "end_seconds": 301.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.43,
      "text": "Book a review after the results are back. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.57,
      "end_seconds": 306.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Okay, so okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.47,
      "end_seconds": 312.72,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look after yourself."
    }
  ]
